course: dictionary
lesson: 7147
title: Percent means out of 100
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word percent is made of two parts: per means for each, and cent means hundred. So percent means out of every hundred. The sign is %. «50 percent» means 50 out of every 100, which is half of the whole.
explain: You meet percent everywhere. A shop might say «20 percent off», and a phone shows its battery in percent. Weather forecasts give a «80 percent chance of rain», and test scores can be shown as percentages too. Each time, the number tells you how many parts out of 100 you have.
explain: Percent works like a fraction with 100 on the bottom. So 25% means 25 out of 100, which can be written as 25/100, and that simplifies to 1/4. If you know that 100% is the whole, you can judge any percentage: 100% is everything, and 1% is a tiny piece.
fact: Percent means out of every hundred, and the sign is %.
fact: «50 percent» means 50 out of 100, which is a half.
fact: 100% means the whole thing.
fact: 10% of 60 is 6, because 10 out of every 100 is one tenth of the amount.
fact: «a hundred percent» means completely, so a percent can describe how much of something is true or done.
exercise: «The shop has 50 percent off all coats.» What does 50 percent mean? | 5 out of every 100 | 50 out of every 10 | *50 out of every 100, which is a half | 500 out of every 100
exercise: What is 25 percent written as a fraction? | 1/25 | 100/25 | *25/100, which is 1/4 | 25/10
exercise: «It's a 1 percent chance, not a 1 percent promise.» What does a 1 percent chance mean? | Half of the time | *Only 1 out of every 100, very unlikely | 1 out of every 10, quite likely | Certain to happen
test: What is 10 percent of 60? | 600 | *6 | 16 | 0.6
test: What does 100 percent mean? | Nothing at all | Half of the whole | *The whole thing | 10 out of 100
exam: «There is an 80 percent chance of rain today.» What does this mean? | Rain is impossible | Only 8 out of every 100 chances | Rain will last 80 minutes | *Rain is very likely: 80 out of every 100 chances
